=46osdem will be held the 4th and 5th of February 2012 in Brussels,
Belgium. As usual and for the 9th time there will be an embedded and
mobile room.

=46or this years program we are looking for people who would like to do
a presentation about their or their community's projects in this area.
These projects must be Free Software or Open Source.

=46or example involvement and experiences with projects like Arduino,
Meego/Tizen, Mer, Beagleboard, Openembedded, Android, OpenWrt, Yocto, L=
inaro...
Also we are interested in short tutorials, project overviews,
achievements, ports to new hardware and hardware hacking, real life dep=
loyments,
=2E..all are welcome and all submissions will be reviewed by our panel.

Submissions require a small abstract and short speaker presentation
and should be submitted to fosdem.embedded@gmail.com.before the 15th of
january of 2012

The panel consists of:

Philippe De Swert
Peter De Schrijver
Klaas Van Gend
Dave Neary
Michael Opdenacker
Geert Uytterhoeven

Looking forward to see you all at Fosdem (http://www.fosdem.org/)!

